.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt GROUPDEL 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm groupdel
.Nd remove a group
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Ar group
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility removes
.Ar group
from
.Pa /etc/group ,
in the shape of the
.Nx
and
.Ox
command.
It is
.Xr pw 8
under another name.
As on
.Ox ,
a group that is some user's primary group is not removed: that user
would be left with a group ID that names nothing.
It must be run by the superuser.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v
Say what was done.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
As
.Xr pw 8 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr group 5 ,
.Xr groupadd 8 ,
.Xr groupmod 8 ,
.Xr pw 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility appeared in
.Nx 1.5
and
.Ox 2.7 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
